 | `render.2d_emit_zip` | `on` | at `render.scale=2`, the output stage (master brightness, 6-to-8-bit expansion) writes straight into the frame's two 512-pixel rows: a 3D line's four composited quarters zipped (even and odd pixels) as it goes, and a line without the 3D layer, or of the bottom screen, with each pixel doubled (`render.2d_fast` builds, display mode 1); `off`: a converted 256-pixel line first, then the zip or the doubling. Same pixels |
 | `render.2d_prefetch` | `off` | at `render.scale=2` with `render.3d_share` and `render.2d_quarters`, the 2D thread prefetches the next line's four 3D quarters (4 KB of Gengis's rows, written on other cores and read once here: the 2D thread's main memory cost at 2x) while it composites this line's. Same pixels; off until the device says it helps (the simulator can't see prefetches) |
+| `render.2d_tiles` | `on` | at `render.scale=2` with `render.2d_quarters` and `render.2d_emit_zip` (display mode 1, `render.2d_fast`), a 3D line's four quarters are composited, given their colour effects and written into the frame's two rows in 64-pixel tiles, so each quarter's composited pixels are read back for the zip while still in L1, instead of four 1 KB lines a pass later. `off`: the whole-line passes. Same pixels |
 | `render.3d_share` | `on` | with Gengis and the 2D thread, a line's job points at Gengis's rows of the 3D frame (Gengis keeps two frames' rows) instead of a copy: at `render.scale=2` the line's four quarters (4 KB), at 1x the line (1 KB). Exact: the same frames and audio |
 | `render.2d_lazy` | `on` | with the 2D thread (`render.2d_thread`), a frame's last lines may be drawn while the emulator runs the next frame: at a frame's end the emulator waits only for the frame before's, and whoever reads a frame (the KMS presenter, `top()`/`bottom()`, a savestate's picture) waits for its own. Same pictures |
 | `render.3d_wait2d` | `on` | with `render.3d_share` (1x and 2x), the 2D thread waits for each line's Gengis bin before compositing it, not the emulator's thread; the emulator waits for the 3D frame only at VBlank (before the geometry engine's next frame; with `render.3d_pipeline` only for its conversion). Same pictures |
